// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a local ANNOTATED at a union ARM (`const c: Circle = { r: n }`) returned
// from an UN-ANNOTATED function, in a module that also declares a standalone struct of that
// arm's exact layout (`Dot`). Eleven lines, no import, no generic, no lambda, no list. `vl
// check` exits 0 — one redundant-annotation HINT, no error — and is the ONLY command that
// misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run`
// exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The message is the stable
// identifier, and the two `$type`s are two DIFFERENT heap types behind one placeholder.)
//
// THE TWIN IS THE TRIGGER AND THE ANNOTATION IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. Controls, each ONE line
// different from this file and each RUN:
//   · `type Dot` DELETED                                     → runs, prints 7   ← the axis
//   · `type Dot = { q: i32 }` (same arity, different field)  → runs, prints 7
//   · `Sq` + `Shape` DELETED, so `Circle` is a plain struct  → runs, prints 7
//   · `function mk(n: i32): Circle` (the RESULT annotated)   → runs, prints 7
//
// So it needs the arm, the exact-layout standalone twin, and an annotation on the VALUE but
// not on the result. The last control is the tell about where the hole is: with the result
// annotated, `synthRetPinAnn` and the annotated-return ladder agree on `uVarHeap[Circle]`;
// with only the local annotated, the local's own cell resolves the arm while the INFERRED
// result valtype takes `Dot`'s row from the structural ladder, and the two are the two
// `$type`s.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, not a regression: silent on master `c0873a06` too, with the same `vl check`
// rc 0 and the same engine message. It is `silent-class-inventory.md` D52, and it is 16 of the
// 20 cells the D39/D40/D41 grid leaves silent. All 20 are `decl=arm`; these 16 are the
// `twin=exact` ones, and the other 4 are this same shape at `twin` none / namediff reachable
// only through `mapIndexed`. Nothing in the silent residue is `ann=result`, which is what says
// the twin is the axis here rather than the annotation POSITION — that half is D39, closed.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `c` is inferred as `{r: i32}`
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }

function mk(n: i32) {
  const c: Circle = { r: n }
  return c
}

print(mk(7).r)
